# Warm the gas, stop before burst
# Predict the pressure order for equal sealed gas samples given 0 J, 100 J,
# 200 J and 400 J. The first three remain measurable; the last crosses the
# vessel boundary. Stop there: a burst is evidence, not an invitation to retry.
register lv2
seal v1 500mL
add v1 N2 0.0042mol
measure v1 pressure
new
seal v2 500mL
add v2 N2 0.0042mol
heat v2 100J
measure v2 pressure
new
seal v3 500mL
add v3 N2 0.0042mol
heat v3 200J
measure v3 pressure
new
seal v4 500mL
add v4 N2 0.0042mol
heat v4 400J
measure v4 pressure
